+-----------------------------------------------------------------------
| Running ${PKGSTEM} on OpenBSD
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------

Confettysh runs an SSH server that plays terminal visual effects for
connecting clients.  It is a public, unauthenticated demonstration
service: anyone who can reach the port can connect and view the effects.
Do not run it on an untrusted network without a packet filter rule.

The rc.d(8) script runs the server as the _confettysh user with
/var/db/confettysh as the working directory.  Host keys are written to
/var/db/confettysh/.ssh and persist across restarts.

	doas rcctl enable confettysh
	doas rcctl start confettysh

The packaged rc.d(8) script listens on 127.0.0.1:2222 and exposes the
Prometheus metrics endpoint on 127.0.0.1:9222.  confettysh performs no
authentication, so do not move it to a public address unless the network
in front of it authenticates and restricts access.  The -listen flag
selects the address for both endpoints; -port and -metrics-port select
their ports.  Override the defaults in /etc/rc.conf.local,
for example:

	confettysh_flags="-listen 127.0.0.1 -port 2222 -metrics-port 9222"

Connect with:

	ssh -p 2222 localhost
